          {
            "id": "asc-1",
            "type": "audio_script",
            "position": {
              "x": 0.0,
              "y": 0.0
            },
            "description": "Per-sample audio-rate YAMS program (one eval per sample). A stereo sine-wavefolder whose fold depth tracks note velocity, with a per-channel one-pole lowpass (state cells) and a self-generated sub-octave (internal phasor) for body — an oscillator, waveshaper and filter in a single node. Not reproducible with the static stock effects. See the script's inline comments.",
            "parameters": {},
            "scripts": {
              "1": "# Stereo sine-wavefolder + self-generated sub-octave.\n# Runs once PER AUDIO SAMPLE — only the audio-rate AudioScript module\n# can do this (per-voice, per-sample DSP: oscillator + shaper + filter\n# all in one node). Harder velocity = deeper fold = brighter timbre.\n\nstate lpl = 0                 # one-pole lowpass memory, left  (persists per sample)\nstate lpr = 0                 # one-pole lowpass memory, right\n\nlet drive = 1 + velocity * 7  # fold depth tracks how hard the note is played\n\nlet fl = sin(in_l * drive)    # sine wavefolding adds harmonics live (left in)\nlet fr = sin(in_r * drive)    # right folded independently -> stereo width\n\nlpl = lpl + 0.35 * (fl - lpl) # one-pole LP tames the fold's brightness/alias\nlpr = lpr + 0.35 * (fr - lpr)\n\nlet f = mtof(note * 127)            # note pitch in Hz (the `note` macro is MIDI/127)\nlet sub = sin(phasor(f * 0.5) * tau) * 0.35  # internal sine one octave down -> body\n\nout.left  = lpl * 0.7 + sub   # folded top mixed with the sub-octave\nout.right = lpr * 0.7 + sub\n"
            }
          }
        ],
